Yes — that is a better long-term architecture. I would make the Chaos platform technology-independent, with a central UI/API/control plane and lightweight client libraries/agents for .NET and Spring Boot.

The key distinction is:

Chaos Control Plane = centralized and technology agnostic
Chaos SDK = embedded into each application
Chaos API = the contract between them

This lets the same simulator control .NET, Java/Spring, and eventually other technologies.

