Application integration

The application should have a very small integration surface:

.NET Application
       │
       ├── Chaos SDK
       │      │
       │      └── calls Chaos API
       │
       ├── Chaos-aware MQ adapter
       ├── Chaos-aware Kafka adapter
       ├── Chaos-aware DB adapter
       └── Chaos-aware Storage adapter

And Spring:

Spring Boot Application
       │
       ├── Chaos Starter
       │      │
       │      └── calls Chaos API
       │
       ├── Chaos-aware MQ adapter
       ├── Chaos-aware Kafka adapter
       ├── Chaos-aware DB adapter
       └── Chaos-aware Storage adapter

One important change to the earlier design

I would not make every injection request synchronously call the Chaos API.

For example, if you process 100,000 transactions:

BAD
Transaction
   ↓
Call Chaos API
   ↓
Evaluate
   ↓
Process transaction

That creates dependency on the Chaos platform and unnecessary latency.

Instead:

Chaos UI
   ↓
Chaos API
   ↓
Configuration
   ↓
.NET/Spring SDK
   ↓
Local configuration cache
   ↓
Fast local evaluation
   ↓
Fault injection

The SDK periodically pulls configuration or receives a configuration notification.

Then:

Evaluate locally
      ↓
condition matches?
      ↓
YES → inject
NO  → normal processing

The SDK reports injection events asynchronously.

This means the Chaos platform can itself be unavailable without breaking the payment application.

