Even better: three levels of injection

I recommend designing the generalized platform around three injection levels.

Level 1 — Application checkpoint

Business operation
      ↓
Chaos SDK
      ↓
Evaluate
      ↓
Inject

Examples:

FILE_PARSE
DB_INSERT
MQ_PUBLISH
MQ_RESPONSE
KAFKA_PUBLISH
KAFKA_CONSUME
SETTLEMENT_MATCH
FILE_WRITE

Level 2 — Infrastructure adapter

Application
     ↓
Chaos-aware adapter
     ↓
Real dependency

Examples:

ChaosAwareHttpClient
ChaosAwareKafkaProducer
ChaosAwareMqClient
ChaosAwareDbClient
ChaosAwareFileStorage

This is ideal for dependency failures.

Level 3 — Kubernetes/OpenShift

Chaos API
     ↓
Kubernetes Adapter
     ↓
Pod

For example:

Restart:
ACH-Prefund-Worker
DC1
Pod #2

This is independent of .NET/Spring.

