I would make one further architectural improvement

Instead of naming the component Chaos Monkey, use something like:

Enterprise Chaos Platform

with these components:

Chaos Control Plane
Chaos Management API
Chaos SDK
Chaos Agent
Chaos Execution Engine
Chaos Adapter
Chaos Simulator
Chaos Assertion Engine
Chaos Reporter

Then the SDK becomes reusable across your organization.

For example:

             Enterprise Chaos Platform
                       │
        ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
        │              │              │
       .NET          Spring        Kubernetes
        │              │              │
       SDK            SDK           Adapter
        │              │
        └───────┬──────┘
                │
          Common Contract
                │
        ┌───────┼────────┐
        ▼       ▼        ▼
       MQ     Kafka     DB

The most important design rule: the application should never depend synchronously on the Chaos Control Plane for normal processing. The SDK should cache the active experiment configuration locally, fail open when Chaos is unavailable, and report injection results asynchronously. That gives you a reusable platform without introducing a new production dependency into your ACH transaction path.
